(TRACE AI Reference Manual - Page 2: API Gateway & 504 Timeout Runbook) Tj
T* (System: api-gateway | Normal Latency: 70-120 ms | SLA Error Rate: < 1%) Tj
T* (Alert Thresholds: latency_ms > 1000 ms \(WARN\), latency_ms > 2000 ms \(CRITICAL\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Symptom: 504 Gateway Timeout on /v1/checkout or /v1/orders with error_rate > 10%.) Tj
T* (Cascade Behavior:) Tj
T* (- When db-proxy reaches 100/100 connections, api-gateway worker threads block) Tj
T* (  waiting for database slots \(wait_ms > 2500\), driving CPU > 85% and latency > 3000ms.) Tj
T* (- If error rate exceeds 40%, the circuit breaker enters half-open state.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Remediation Steps:) Tj
T* (- Relieve upstream DB lock or pool saturation first.) Tj
T* (- Perform a rolling restart of api-gateway worker pool to clear blocked threads.) Tj
T* (- Confirm circuit breaker closes and latency returns below 150 ms.) Tj
ET
endstream
